---The loaded planetary system.
---@class ksa.SystemInfo
---@field name string The system name.
---@field home string? The id of the home body, or nil.
---@field sun string? The id of the sun, or nil.

---The outcome of a write. `ok` is true exactly when `outcome` is `"Ok"`.
---@class ksa.CommandResult
---@field ok boolean Whether the command applied.
---@field outcome "Ok"|"Invalid"|"NotFound"|"Denied"|"Busy"|"Fault"|"TimedOut"|"Unsupported" `Ok`; `Invalid` (bad argument); `NotFound` (the vessel or module vanished); `Denied` (control disabled in the config); `Busy` (cannot fire right now); `Fault` (a game API failed); `TimedOut` (the game thread did not run it in time); `Unsupported` (disabled after a fault, or not available).
---@field message string? A human-readable detail, or nil.

---Timing of one simulation step.
---@class ksa.StepInfo
---@field ut number Universal time at the step, in seconds.
---@field dt number Duration of the step, in seconds.
---@field step_index number The simulation step counter.
---@field frame number The rendered frame counter.

---A game event as delivered to hooks and returned by `wait_event`.
---@class ksa.EventInfo
---@field ut number Universal time when the event was raised, in seconds.
---@field type ksa.EventName|string The event name.
---@field vessel_id string? The vessel the event concerns, or nil.
---@field payload table<string, any> Event-specific fields; see the `Events` interface for each event's payload.

---A registered hook. Hooks are removed automatically when the script unloads or reloads.
---@class ksa.Subscription
---@field id string The subscription id.
local Subscription = {}

---Removes the hook. Safe to call more than once.
function Subscription:unsubscribe() end

---The cancellation signal of a service, main or terminal script.
---@class ksa.Signal
---@field cancelled boolean True once the script is being stopped or reloaded; long-running loops should check it.
local Signal = {}

---Runs `fn` when the script is being stopped.
---@param fn fun() Called once on cancellation.
function Signal:on_cancel(fn) end

---Persistent per-script state, saved in the save game's sidecar and restored on load. Values must be plain data (numbers, strings, booleans, lists, maps); a stored value is returned exactly as it was stored.
---@class ksa.State
local State = {}

---Reads a stored value; nil when the key is unset.
---@param key string The state key.
---@return any
function State.get(key) end

---Stores a value; storing nil clears the key.
---@param key string The state key.
---@param value any The value to store.
function State.set(key, value) end

---Logging and game console access (`ksa.console`, also `ctx.log`). Arguments are joined with a space; non-strings are formatted readably.
---@class ksa.Console
local Console = {}

---Writes an info line to the mod log and the in-game console.
---@param ... any Values to print.
function Console.log(...) end

---Writes an info line (same as `log`).
---@param ... any Values to print.
function Console.info(...) end

---Writes a warning line.
---@param ... any Values to print.
function Console.warn(...) end

---Writes an error line.
---@param ... any Values to print.
function Console.error(...) end

---Writes a debug line (hidden unless the log level allows it).
---@param ... any Values to print.
function Console.debug(...) end

---Runs a game console command, as if typed into the in-game console.
---@param command string The console command line.
function Console.exec(command) end

---Identifies the running script.
---@class ksa.ScriptInfo
---@field name string The script name.
---@field path string The script's file path.

---A script-owned virtual terminal (`ctx.term`), rendered by purrTTY in a window or on a part. Write ANSI escape sequences, read keyboard and mouse bytes. Output is buffered and flushed once per step slot.
---@class ksa.Terminal
---@field size { cols: number, rows: number } The current grid: the smallest attached surface. Re-read it after a `resize` event.
---@field attached number The number of surfaces (windows or part quads) attached to this terminal.
local Terminal = {}

---Appends output to the terminal (a string).
---@param data string The text or bytes to write.
function Terminal.write(data) end

---Waits for the next chunk of input (keys, mouse reports, terminal replies) and returns its bytes as a string.
---@async
---@return string
function Terminal.read() end

---Push-style input: calls `fn` with the event payload. `resize` carries `{ cols, rows }`, `data` carries `{ data }`.
---@param event "data"|"resize"|"attach"|"detach"|"cancel" The terminal event.
---@param fn fun(payload: table) Called with the event payload.
---@return ksa.Subscription
function Terminal.on(event, fn) end

---Clears the screen and homes the cursor.
function Terminal.clear() end

---Does nothing: output is flushed automatically once per step slot. Kept for symmetry with real terminals.
function Terminal.flush() end

---Sets the terminal window title.
---@param s string The title.
function Terminal.title(s) end

---Sets the terminal lifecycle policy.
---@param opts { stop_when_detached: boolean } `stop_when_detached` stops the script when the last surface closes (default: keep running and buffer output).
function Terminal.policy(opts) end

---What every hook and entry point receives as its only argument.
---@class ksa.BaseContext
---@field ksa ksa The ksa module (the same object as the global).
---@field script ksa.ScriptInfo The running script.
---@field log ksa.Console The console, for logging (same as `ksa.console`).
---@field kind string Which kind of invocation this is: `"event"`, `"tick"`, `"service"`, `"main"` or `"terminal"`.

---The context of an event hook.
---@class ksa.EventContext : ksa.BaseContext
---@field event ksa.EventInfo The event.
---@field vessel ksa.VesselRef? The vessel the event concerns, or nil.
---@field sync boolean True when the hook runs inline inside the game call that raised the event (it must not wait).
---@field ut number Universal time of the event (copy of `event.ut`).
---@field type ksa.EventName|string The event name (copy of `event.type`).
---@field vessel_id string? The vessel id, or nil (copy of `event.vessel_id`).
---@field payload table<string, any> The event payload (copy of `event.payload`).

---The context of a per-frame, per-step or interval hook.
---@class ksa.TickContext : ksa.BaseContext
---@field ut number Universal time, in seconds.
---@field dt number Duration of the step (or frame), in seconds.
---@field step_index number The simulation step counter.
---@field frame number The rendered frame counter.

---The context of a service or main entry point.
---@class ksa.ServiceContext : ksa.BaseContext
---@field signal ksa.Signal Becomes cancelled when the script is stopped or reloaded.
---@field term ksa.Terminal? The script's virtual terminal when it owns one; nil otherwise. Terminal scripts use TerminalContext, where it is always present.

---The context of a terminal script: a service that also owns a virtual terminal.
---@class ksa.TerminalContext : ksa.ServiceContext
---@field term ksa.Terminal The script's virtual terminal.

---The context of a script's `main` entry point (the same as a service context).
---@class ksa.MainContext : ksa.ServiceContext

return ksa
